

#  Lambda Expressions

   Lambda is an Anonymous function, means it does not belong to any class and do not have any name.
   ( Function with a name )
   Lambda expression is mainly used to implements functional interfaces.

## Functional Interface

   An interface that contains exactly one abstract method  is known as a functional interface.

       interface MyFunctionalInterface{
          public void execute();
       }

       by default it is abstract.
       Abstract -> a method with no implementation

   Functional interface can have any number of default, static method but c an contain only one abstract method.

### Lambda vs Method

    Method is always belongs to class or objects in java where as Lambda does not belong to any class or objects.
    Method has the main parts;
    - Name
    - Parameter List
    - Body
    - Return Type

    public int addition ( int a, int b){
       return a + b ;
    }

    Lambda Expression main parts;
    - No Name ( As Lambda is an anonymous function so no need to have a name)
    - Parameter List
    - Body ( This is the main part of the function)
    - No Return Type
